      "source_groundedness": 0.95,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Raw word count is a generic surface feature with little clinical explanatory leverage for the query and is near-constant (18-30, tightly clustered). Values are trivially derivable and accurate, but analytical value is low."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.68,
  "source_groundedness": 0.78,
  "rationale": "Most added columns supply genuine clinical axes (procedures/orders, chronic burden, case complexity, referrals, medications) that plausibly explain visit duration and enable grouping/modeling. Groundedness is generally acceptable but weakened by inflated systems_involved_count values (e.g. 4 systems for an annual physical) and some liberal readings of 'procedure performed'. note_word_count is well grounded but adds little analytical leverage for this query, dragging the holistic usefulness down."
